# Security headers applied by the Workers Static Assets layer to every asset
# response. Worker routes (/api/*) set their own headers in code. The
# @astrojs/cloudflare adapter appends its /_astro/* cache rule at build time.
#
# CSP notes: Astro emits scoped styles as inline <style> blocks, hence
# style-src 'unsafe-inline'. JSON-LD <script type="application/ld+json"> is
# non-executing data and exempt from script-src. The two sha256 hashes allow
# Astro's inline island-bootstrap scripts (astro-island custom element +
# directive loader) — they change on Astro upgrades; the /ask e2e suite fails
# closed if they drift. Regenerate: build, then hash each inline <script> in
# dist/client/ask.html (sha256, base64). connect-src 'self' covers the
# island's /api/ask call. manifest-src 'self' is required for the
# <link rel="manifest"> in BaseLayout — without it the manifest falls back to
# default-src 'none' and the browser blocks it (Lighthouse best-practices
# flags the CSP console error).
#
# Permissions-Policy disables only real, recognised hardware features. No
# ad-tech opt-out tokens (interest-cohort, browsing-topics, …): FLoC is dead,
# the Privacy Sandbox set is being retired, and browsers log an
# "Unrecognized feature" console warning for each stale token.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-eIXWvAmxkr251LJZkjniEK5LcPF3NkapbJepohwYRIc=' 'sha256-Ya0pUYrC7nM5Cn/056TyVuEiz6dFGrzmkWzgON0pF0U='; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
